; The collision for this pipe is a ring of 16 convex boxes, not the
; ConcavePolygonShape3D that used to live in pipe_collision.tres. That trimesh
; was baked from the .blend and could not be trusted: probing it reported
; contacts in the middle of a bore that ray casts proved empty (it is a clean
; 1.50 m cylinder), and a turtle whose box ended up low in the tube was frozen
; solid -- 6 s with no forward progress and 0.00 m of response to the swim key,
; because move_and_slide cannot depenetrate a body out of a concave surface.
;
; Convex pieces fix both halves of that. The bore is now exactly defined by these
; numbers rather than by whatever triangles the bake produced, and every piece
; can push a body back out, so the worst case is a nudge instead of a dead stop.
; tools/probe_pipe_clearance.gd checks the bore and drives the real controller
; through the pipe.
[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="tube_seg"]
size = Vector3(0.5, 7.62, 0.7169)

[sub_resource type="SphereMesh" id="bub_mesh"]
radius = 0.05
height = 0.1

[sub_resource type="Gradient" id="bub_grad"]
